---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Flag from "../components/Flag.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { legs, totals } from "../data/walk.js";

const count = legs.reduce((n, l) => n + l.stops.length, 0);
const badge = { open: "Just walk up", ask: "You have to ask first", maybe: "Nobody has checked yet" };
let stopNo = 0;
---
<Base title="The walk" dek="Every place in this website that is still standing, in the order you could actually go and see them — nineteen stops, six countries, and it ends at your own front door.">

  <div class="hero" style="text-align:left">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker" style="--c:var(--croatia)">One trip, ten families</div>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(38px,7vw,70px)">Walk along the line</h1>
      <p class="lead big">Almost everything in this website is a place you could stand in. Here they
      all are, in the order you could actually do them — and the last stop is your own front door.</p>
      <p class="lead">This is not in date order. It is a route. It starts in London because two
      families walked out of England and never came back, and it finishes in Brisbane because that
      is where every single line in this story arrives.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="nums g4">
        {totals.map(t => (
          <div class="num">
            <b>{t.label === "stops" ? count : t.n}</b><span>{t.label}</span><i>{t.sub}</i>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What the three labels mean</h2>
      <p class="lead">The grown-up archives keep itineraries like this for researchers, and they are
      strict about one thing: never say a place is there when nobody has checked. So every stop
      below carries one of these.</p>
      <div class="keys">
        <div class="keyrow"><span class="acc open">Just walk up</span>
          <p>It is standing, it is public, and it costs nothing.</p></div>
        <div class="keyrow"><span class="acc ask">You have to ask first</span>
          <p>An archive or an office holds it. Somebody has to let you in, usually weeks ahead.</p></div>
        <div class="keyrow"><span class="acc maybe">Nobody has checked yet</span>
          <p>It should be there. No one in this family has stood in front of it to make sure.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {legs.map(leg => (
    <section class="legsec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="leghead">
          <svg width="46" height="34" viewBox="0 -6 40 34" aria-hidden="true">
            <Flag id={`leg${leg.n}`} kind={leg.flag} x={2} y={2} />
            <rect x="0" y="-6" width="2" height="34" fill="var(--ink-3)" />
          </svg>
          <div>
            <div class="legno">Leg {leg.n}</div>
            <h2>{leg.name}</h2>
            <div class="legsub">{leg.sub} · {leg.km}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="lead">{leg.lead}</p>

        <ol class="walk">
          {leg.stops.map(s => {
            stopNo += 1;
            return (
              <li class={`stop c-${s.k} ${s.last ? "is-last" : ""}`}>
                <div class="pin"><b>{stopNo}</b></div>
                <div class="card">
                  <h3>{s.place}</h3>
                  <div class="land">{s.land}</div>
                  <span class={`acc ${s.access}`}>{badge[s.access]}</span>
                  <p>{s.what}</p>
                  <div class="still"><b>Still there:</b> {s.see}</div>
                  <div class="lookfor"><b>Look for:</b> {s.look}</div>
                </div>
              </li>
            );
          })}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="callout" style="--c:var(--sun);--cw:#FFF7DF;--cd:#7A5B00">
        <h3>🚶 And the honest bit</h3>
        <p>Nobody has done this whole walk. Bits of it have been done — the archive at Pazin sent
        pages out in 2021, the wall grave at Senj has been photographed twice, the Burgersdorp
        stone has been read. Most of the rest is standing there being unvisited. If you ever go to
        one of them, photograph it properly and write down the date, because that is exactly how
        every fact on this website got here in the first place.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pager">
        <a href={u("/places/")}>← What those places are like</a>
        <a href={u("/journeys/")}>How they got here →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
